        -:   59:/**
        -:   60: * Conditionally flashed vias and pads that interact with zones of different priority can be
        -:   61: * very squirrelly.
        -:   62: *
        -:   63: * In particular, when filling a higher-priority zone that does -not- connect to a via/pad, we
        -:   64: * don't know whether or not a lower-priority zone will subsequently connect -- so we can't
        -:   65: * determine clearance because we don't know what the final flashing state will be.
        -:   66: *
        -:   67: * We therefore force the flashing state if the highest-priority zone with the same net -can-
        -:   68: * connect (whether or not it does in the end), and otherwise force the zone-connection state
        -:   69: * to no-connection (even though a lower priority zone -might- have otherwise connected to it.
        -:   70: */
        -:   71:enum ZONE_LAYER_OVERRIDE
        -:   72:{
        -:   73:    ZLO_NONE,
        -:   74:    ZLO_FORCE_FLASHED,
        -:   75:    ZLO_FORCE_NO_ZONE_CONNECTION
        -:   76:};
